# --- Operator-local state: NEVER commit -----------------------------------
# Real keys, station URLs and admin credentials.
.env
# Panel-written settings, API keys (plaintext!), and logs.
data/
# Contains your real LiveKit keypair (copy from livekit.example.yaml).
livekit.yaml
# Names your personas and voice samples (copy from persona-voices.example.json).
agent-worker/persona-voices.json

# --- Binaries and environments ---------------------------------------------
.venv/
bin/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Internal working notes, not part of the release -----------------------
MASTER-PLAN.md
AUDIT.md
REVIEW.md
RELEASE-REVIEW-1.0.md
BUILD-INSTRUCTIONS.md
talkwave-panel-spec.md
# Drafts of requests to file upstream — they go stale the moment the
# issue is filed, and one reached a public branch by being the only
# working note here without a rule (0.10.99).
UPSTREAM-REQUEST-*.md
# Session handovers: written for whoever picks the work up next, and they
# name the operator's own box. Same rule as the drafts above.
HANDOVER*.md
subwave-openapi.json
# Design handoff bundles (the brand-mark zip and any successor). The shipped
# assets are committed in web-widget/ and docs/; the bundle is the working
# source that produced them, and it stays on the operator's machine.
*.zip
# Worked-off notes retire here rather than sitting beside the live ones
# looking like open work (the three audit docs moved 2026-08-11, ~95% done,
# survivors folded into the tracked backlog first).
notes-archive/

*.log

# --- Claude Code ------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent instructions and skills are part of the repo: they are how a fresh
# checkout (or a fresh agent) learns this codebase without re-reading it. Only
# machine-local overrides stay out. This repo is public and deliberately
# sanitized: anything naming the operator's own hosts, IPs or keys goes in a
# *.local.md file, never in a committed skill.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.md
# Preview-launcher entries are per-machine scaffolding (the verify skill adds
# and removes its stub entry per session); tracking it shipped one session's
# leftovers to everybody (untracked 0.10.81).
.claude/launch.json

# Headless-Chrome scratch from the live-call harness and the layout probes
# (tools/livecall). A 171MB browser profile reached the repo root once and
# sat there untracked for days, one careless `git add -A` from a permanent
# commit to a public repo.
chromeprofile*/
chrome*.log
